ument Key**: DOC-2048\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-18)\\n\\n## What Was Tested\\n\\nRetrospective note on the packaged Electron+CLI desktop build tested 2026-08-18, exercising the IPC bridge that connects the Electron frontend to the underlying batch CLI engine (T003) for a drag-and-drop batch of 100 PDFs.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-48\\n\\n# Evaluation Note: Electron GUI Wrapper — Package Test\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2048\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-18)\\n\\n## Result: Package Test Passes\\n\\nThe packaged build launches, accepts a dropped folder, invokes the batch CLI over IPC, and returns completed output files correctly. The IPC bridge to the already-completed batch CLI (T003) works as designed — this is accepted as Completed for T035 as of 2026-08-18.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-48\\n\\n# Evaluation Note: Electron GUI Wrapper — Package Test\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2048\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-18)\\n\\n## Known Rough Edge (Not Blocking)\\n\\nProgress-bar feedback during the run is uneven: because the CLI's `stdout` buffer doesn't flush at a steady cadence under heavy load (e.g., OCR-heavy pages), the UI progress indicator jumps rather than moving smoothly. This is a UX polish item, not a functional defect — the batch completes correctly regardless of how the progress bar animates.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-48\\n\\n# Evaluation Note: Electron GUI Wrapper — Package Test\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2048\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-18)\\n\\n## Possible Follow-up\\n\\nA lightweight local WebSocket channel for structured progress events (instead of `stdout` parsing) would smooth this out, but it's not required for the package test to pass and is not currently scheduled.\\n\\n*Status*: Completed. Package test passes; progress-bar smoothness is a tracked but non-blocking follow-up.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 48 evalu note electron gui wrapper packag test owner diana document key doc 2048 last updat 2026 0831 retrospect cover 2026 08 18 what wa test retrospect note on the packag electron cli desktop build test 2026 08 18 exercis the ipc bridg that connect the electron frontend to the under batch cli engin t003 for a drag and drop batch of 100 pdfs sourc id src gdoc 48 evalu note electron gui wrapper packag test owner diana document key doc 2048 last updat 2026 0831 retrospect cover 2026 08 18 result packag test pass the packag build launch accept a drop folder invok the batch cli over ipc and return complet output file correct the ipc bridg to the alreadi complet batch cli t003 work a design this is accept a complet for t035 a of 2026 08 18 sourc id src gdoc 48 evalu note electron gui wrapper packag test owner diana document key doc 2048 last updat 2026 0831 retrospect cover 2026 08 18 known rough edg not block progress bar feedback dure the run is uneven becaus the cli s stdout buffer doesn t flush at a steadi cadenc under heavi load e g ocr heavi page the ui progress indic jump rather than move smooth this is a ux polish item not a function defect the batch complet correct regardless of how the progress bar anim sourc id src gdoc 48 evalu note electron gui wrapper packag test owner diana document key doc 2048 last updat 2026 0831 retrospect cover 2026 08 18 possibl follow up a lightweight local websocket channel for structur progress event instead of stdout pars would smooth this out but it s not requir for the packag test to pas and is not current schedul status complet packag test pass progress bar smooth is a track but non block follow up\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d6752a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-31-GUI-Desktop-Wrapper-Evaluation.md\", \"id\": \"740de53d2a3e3c16\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27333455435844545, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07438016622635064, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73756146, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-31-GUI-Desktop-Wrapper-Evaluation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d6752a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-31-GUI-Desktop-Wrapper-Evaluation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-31-GUI-Desktop-Wrapper-Evaluation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1458, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:07\", \"token_count\": 531, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Background: Path Fix Cleared Packaging\\n\\nBackslash path-handling defects that previously broke Windows builds were fixed on 2026-08-10, and a Windows build artifact was successfully produced by 2026-08-12. Packaging itself is no longer the blocker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Current Blocker: Missing Code-Signing Certificate\\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate procurement is the sole open blocker.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 background path fix clear packag backslash path handl defect that previous broke window build were fix on 2026 08 10 and a window build artifact wa success produc by 2026 08 12 packag itself is no longer the blocker sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 current blocker miss code sign certif the produc build artifact is unsign which trigger a smartscreen warn and defend flag the binari a untrust impact site it polici common block execut of unsign smartscreen flag binari outright which would prevent instal on target deploy workstat without a manual secur polici overrid root caus no code sign certif ha been procur or configur in the window build pipelin yet sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 path to resolut procur a code sign certif and wire sign into the releas build step is the onli remain item befor this clear the t029 window compat gate and by extens the t011 releas checklist which is hold on this exact sign gap alongsid the t005 imag slim down audit status activ build produc success sign certif procur is the sole open blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"7d9dbdfb5b6d7c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2708929943779028, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07024793482557544, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7390648, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1340, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 387, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-40\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Title**: Audit third-party licenses before release\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAudit third-party licenses across the dependency tree before release. An initial audit led to swapping the PDF parser library, but the task was reopened when the replacement parser turned out to be AGPL-licensed; the team is now searching for an Apache/MIT-licensed alternative.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-40\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Title**: Audit third-party licenses before release\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Full dependency tree is audited for license compliance.\\n\\n- No restrictive copyleft (e.g., AGPL) licenses remain in the shipped dependency set.\\n\\n- Apache/MIT-licensed PDF parser alternative is identified and adopted, resolving the reopened AGPL finding.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-40\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Title**: Audit third-party licenses before release\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAudit third-party licenses across the dependency tree before release. An initial audit led to swapping the PDF parser library, but the task was reopened when the replacement parser turned out to be AGPL-licensed; the team is now searching for an Apache/MIT-licensed alternative.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-40\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-40\\n\\n**Title**: Audit third-party licenses before release\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-08**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task for a license compliance review ahead of release.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-15**: Charlie - Apache/MIT Search (Active (Reopened))\\n\\n - *Searching for an Apache/MIT-licensed alternative PDF parser after the task was reopened when the replacement parser turned out to be AGPL-licensed.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 40 sourc id src cu ciph 40 task id ciph 40 titl audit third parti licens befor releas status activ reopen assigne diana prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 descript audit third parti licens across the depend tree befor releas an initi audit led to swap the pdf parser librari but the task wa reopen when the replac parser turn out to be agpl licens the team is now search