License-Compliance-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-40-License-Compliance-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1155, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:35\", \"token_count\": 555, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-47\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Title**: Async job scheduler for concurrent batch API work\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd an asynchronous job scheduler to the batch API for higher throughput under concurrent load. Async workers were added, but a concurrent I/O race was found to cut throughput by roughly 10%; the task is blocked, depending on the multi-threading work.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-47\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Title**: Async job scheduler for concurrent batch API work\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Async job scheduler processes batch API jobs concurrently without a throughput regression.\\n\\n- Concurrent I/O race condition is resolved (currently the blocking issue).\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-47\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Title**: Async job scheduler for concurrent batch API work\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd an asynchronous job scheduler to the batch API for higher throughput under concurrent load. Async workers were added, but a concurrent I/O race was found to cut throughput by roughly 10%; the task is blocked, depending on the multi-threading work.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-47\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Title**: Async job scheduler for concurrent batch API work\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-18**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because an async batch API scheduler is needed for higher throughput.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-25**: Diana - I/O Race Block (Blocked)\\n\\n - *Blocked after finding a concurrent I/O race that cuts throughput by roughly 10%, depending on the multi-threading work.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript add an asynchron job schedul to the batch api for higher throughput under concurr load async worker were ad but a concurr i o race wa found to cut throughput by rough 10 the task is block depend on the multi thread work clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 accept criterion async job schedul process batch api job concurr without a throughput regress concurr i o race condit is resolv current the block issu clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript add an asynchron job schedul to the batch api for higher throughput under concurr load async worker were ad but a concurr i o race wa found to cut throughput by rough 10 the task is block depend on the multi thread work clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 activ histori 2026 08 18 alic task creat open open the task becaus an async batch api schedul is need for higher throughput 2026 08 25 diana i o race block block block after find a concurr i o race that cut throughput by rough 10 depend on the multi thread work\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e991efae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"id\": \"cd124151c990e01e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26342168239736014, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0661157034248002, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7238023, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e991efae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1019, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:06\", \"token_count\": 519, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Original Finding: Ghostscript (AGPLv3)\\n\\nThe initial audit flagged `Ghostscript`, used by the `rasterizer` module for PDF-to-image conversion, as AGPLv3-licensed — on the corporate license blacklist because of its viral copyleft terms for any binary distributed to partner sites.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## First Remediation and Reopen\\n\\nThe team swapped in an alternative PDF parser library to replace the Ghostscript dependency, and that swap was initially marked Completed. On follow-up review, however, the replacement library itself turned out to also be AGPL-licensed — the swap solved the specific Ghostscript dependency but reintroduced the same license category problem one layer down. The task was reopened.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Current Status: Unresolved\\n\\nCharlie is now searching for an Apache 2.0 or MIT-licensed PDF parser alternative that meets the module's rasterization requirements. No suitable replacement has been confirmed yet, so this audit item remains **Active (Reopened)** — not resolved.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Secondary Open Item\\n\\nTesseract OCR itself is Apache 2.0, but the `eng.traineddata` model files were sourced from a community repository and their training-corpus provenance has not been verified as public-domain/CC0. This remains a separate, lower-priority open item pending Evan's trace of the `tessdata_best` provenance.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 origin find ghostscript agplv3 the initi audit flag ghostscript use by the raster modul for pdf to imag convers a agplv3 licens on the corpor licens blacklist becaus of it viral copyleft term for ani binari distribut to partner site sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens 